A||||5||80's BOY||Overbore for your Throttle Body??||||3||
Z||000000||80's BOY||06-02-2000||12:58 PM||||has anyone ever thought of taking your throttle body to a machinist and having it bore out to a larger diameter?? i know that aftermarket t.b. units are very expensive. another thing is, does it really make a difference?? can you gain h.p. either way?? i've seen ricers do it in magazines, along with extrude honing the upper plenums. what do ya'll think??||||reg||3
Z||000001||Alex4mula||06-02-2000||01:55 PM||||Have been done long time ago. Fiero Store sells an unit for $199. Darrel Morse does it for $150 including the plenum. I did mine with him. Very nice job and he even includes new TBS and GM plenum gaskets. TBS alone adds 2 to 4HP as per someone here who dynoed it in a 2.8. It will depend on engine and mods. I hope to get more in my 3.4 with headers and ported intake.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||06-03-2000||01:55 AM||||What you notice is that there is a bigger hole at a lower throttle position. You get the same effect by pressing on the throttle more. Unless you are going to suck or blow more air into the engine, there isn't much to gain.<P>IMHO||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||06-03-2000||02:08 AM||||Hey, my dad is a machinest.  What exactly do you have to bore?||||reg||1
Z||000004||DiggityDan||06-03-2000||03:00 AM||||I know on my dodge conquest, which has the turbo 2.6 4 cyl, there's a guy that sells bored throttle bodies to 10 and 15 mm over. It makes a hell of a difference, but again, it is turbocharged. I agree, I can't see much difference on a nat. aspirated car. Maybe a little if you had the whole intake system worked extrude honed and added more fuel. But you also have to upgrade the plate in the throttle body to a bigger size to fill in the gap left in the tb. wouldn't be hard, might be worth looking into, especially if you could bore it out more than 3mm||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||06-03-2000||03:12 AM||||I have a bored out TB on my V-6. The only difference I find is the car is better over 2000 rpm and up. Below 2000 it feels the same. I did a 0-60 test on the car and it improved it by .2 seconds. I have not dyno'd it yet so I don't know the exact gains. A guess using the 0-60 times was about 5-6HP gain. The car was originally dyno'd with the stock engine and I have made changes to the exhaust, Ignition, injectors, and the larger TB. If I get a chance to dyno it I'll post the difference with a list of all the mods. I did have to port the intake for the TB to flow properly. It's bored out 3mm.||||reg||1
